decision_effect:
No leaky 'static is needed, so the §3.12 'Reverse' trigger (q4-001) did not fire and B2 stands. Two non-leaky designs work. The F7 streaming extension should take the host-driven shape (D2), the only design that covers all four features and also rejects a stale grant across messages and a transaction held open across the response. Proposed F7 extension text (sync, core/alloc only, app crates stay tokio-free):

/// One pull of a host-driven stream.
pub enum Step<T> { Item(T), Idle, Done }

/// Host-owned generator. 'static so it can hold no request-scoped capability; the host mints a fresh Ctx<'m> and db view for every step, after re-checking the session.
pub trait StreamGen: Send + 'static {
    type Item: Send + 'static;
    fn next<'m, D: TenantDb<'m>>(&mut self, ctx: Ctx<'m>, db: &D) -> Result<Step<Self::Item>, SdkError>;
}
pub trait BodyHandler: Send + Sync + 'static {
    type Gen: StreamGen<Item = Chunk>;
    fn open<'r, D: TenantDb<'r>>(&self, ctx: Ctx<'r>, db: &D) -> Result<Self::Gen, SdkError>;
}
pub trait SseHandler: Send + Sync + 'static {
    type Gen: StreamGen<Item = Event>;
    fn open<'r, D: TenantDb<'r>>(&self, ctx: Ctx<'r>, db: &D, last_event_id: Option<u64>) -> Result<Self::Gen, SdkError>;
}
pub enum WsReply { Send(Vec<WsMsg>), Close }
pub trait WsSession: Send + 'static {
    fn on_message<'m, D: TenantDb<'m>>(&mut self, ctx: Ctx<'m>, db: &D, msg: &WsMsg) -> Result<WsReply, SdkError>;
}
pub trait WsHandler: Send + Sync + 'static {
    type Session: WsSession;
    fn open<'r, D: TenantDb<'r>>(&self, ctx: Ctx<'r>, db: &D) -> Result<Self::Session, SdkError>;
}
/// Detached job: a 'static value; the host runs it later with a freshly minted job-scoped Ctx<'j> and denies it if the originating session was revoked.
pub trait Job: Send + 'static {
    fn run<'j, D: TenantDb<'j>>(self, ctx: Ctx<'j>, db: &D) -> Result<(), SdkError>;
}
impl<'r> Ctx<'r> {
    /// Only after commit (INV-NOMUT-C): requires the committed-transaction proof.
    pub fn detach<J: Job>(&self, after: &Tx<'r, Committed>, job: J) -> Result<(), SdkError>;
}

Host obligations (F7 docs plus an adapter-host oracle): mint Ctx/db per step, message and job, never once per session; re-check session liveness before each step and fail closed (Unavailable); drop or deny queued jobs whose session is revoked; idle/step budget per stream. Chunk/Event/WsMsg are SDK newtypes (bytes / {id, data} / text|binary). Clippy ban list unchanged (spawn family, Box::leak, mem::forget, OnceLock/static Mutex). D1 (borrowing Sink<'r>) is not frozen: it also has no 'static escape but accepts E14/E15 and cannot detach. Not applied to F7 by this spike (spec author re-freezes).
